From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: make FmpDxe FV-resident

UefiPayloadPkg builds FmpDxe under CAPSULE_SUPPORT but lists only EsrtDxe
in the FDF, because upstream expects FmpDxe to travel inside the capsule
as an embedded driver. This platform builds with SECURE_BOOT_ENABLE=TRUE,
and coreboot's own Kconfig warns that an embedded driver must then be
signed by a key the running firmware trusts or capsule processing fails.

Putting FmpDxe in the firmware volume sidesteps embedded-driver signing
entirely and matches how the RPi5 platform in this fleet does it.

The FDF's FmpDxe entry must carry the same FILE_GUID override the DSC
applies under CAPSULE_SUPPORT ($(CAPSULE_MAIN_FW_GUID)) -- a bare INF
statement pulls in FmpDxe under its default FILE_GUID
(78EF0A56-1CF0-4535-B5DA-F6FD2F405A11), which GenFv never generates an
FFS for, since the DSC's <Defines> override redirects the build output to
d25f89e1-94ec-4533-80b9-7f8855ce0a94 instead. FDF INF statements parse
FILE_GUID as a literal registry-format GUID or a named GUID from a .dec
file (BaseTools GenFds/FdfParser.py, _GetInfOptions -> _GetNextGuid); they
do not expand $(...) macros at that grammar position, so the literal is
used here, with a comment tying it back to the DSC's CAPSULE_MAIN_FW_GUID.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform policy]

---

diff --git aa/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf bb/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf
--- aa/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf
+++ bb/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf
@@ -426,6 +426,9 @@
 # Capsules
 #
 !if $(CAPSULE_SUPPORT) == TRUE
+# FILE_GUID must track this DSC's CAPSULE_MAIN_FW_GUID define. FDF INF
+# statements only accept a literal GUID here, not a $(...) macro.
+INF FILE_GUID = d25f89e1-94ec-4533-80b9-7f8855ce0a94 FmpDevicePkg/FmpDxe/FmpDxe.inf
 INF MdeModulePkg/Universal/EsrtDxe/EsrtDxe.inf
 !endif
 
